WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:08.780
At the Göbsi peak near Gonten in Switzerlandand 1200 meters above sea level, two artists

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.809
have set up a bed.

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:22.230
The walls and roof are absent.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:28.280
The Hotel with no stars was dreamt up by twin brothers Frank and Patrick Riklin.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.530
“The interesting thing about the hotel is
that many people don't know what it is.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.080
Is it art, tourism or innovation?

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:43.550
The most exciting thing about it is that we
make people a bit uncertain.”

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:49.980
Forget wallpaper, the scenery around this bed is the draw for visitors from all over the world.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:57.440
We designed this bed, built it and opened
up shop - and it's been "no vacanies" ever since.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:03.260
“Turning the tables is part of the gag ... zero stars, doesn't mean bare-bones basics.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.679
Instead, it's about experiencing a whole new kind of luxury.”

00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:12.780
Farmer Köbi Dietrich didn't have much to
do with art -- until now.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.840
Now he works as a consierge and butler.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:23.529
“At first I didn't think this would involve
me so much, but I'm pleased to be part of

00:01:23.529 --> 00:01:25.200
this bed idea.”

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:34.039
After milking the cows every evening, the
alm farmer dresses up for art.

00:01:34.039 --> 00:01:47.530
“The idea was to figure out how to shape
the concept -- which is art, of course -- and  bring it to life so the players, the people who live around this artwork, become part of it.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.939
Without him, it would be far too conventional.

00:01:51.939 --> 00:01:56.579
He jumps and hops or “slips is right.

00:01:56.579 --> 00:01:58.729
Slips right into this artwork.

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:02.150
Speaking as an artist, the project is like
a painting, but it's alive.”

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:08.990
A lonely farmer, who spends the summer on the mountain apasture with only his wife,

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:13.460
children and cows for company is enjoying the constant flow of visitors.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:19.180
“There've been two marriage proposals.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:24.470
One came in a helicopter.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:25.470
That gave me goosebumps.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.790
It was really touching, and then agreed to
marry him.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:35.330
I've never been able to experience so closely what I see here now."

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:49.680
A night at the hotel costs about 270 euros, alpine views and breakfast included.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.580
The new guests have arrived.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:58.880
The two friends from Geneva were able to step in when a vacancy opened at the last minute.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:06.780
They're the first guests to meet the artists
in person.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:13.050
“I think it is the best idea in the world.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.260
It is amazing.”

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.430
The two feel at home right away.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.180
Raphael Tamman's drone hovers above them to immortalize their "mountain high."

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.180
“It's brilliant.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:28.900
I was the one who said we should come here.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.710
And now we've got this sunset to look at.”

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:37.210
“Who else is gone asleep like this, in the
middle of the most beautiful mountains of  the world, with a sunset like that.”

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.960
"I can't even realize yet.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.920
I think I need a bit of time.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.270
It's unreal, it's unreal.”

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:48.790
Entertainment is analogue and consists of watching the weather, telling jokes or listening

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:56.740
to music.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:00.760
It's an artistic critique of the digitization
craze.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.819
The guests are the stars at this hotel.

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:11.770
“When you see how people react, how they move around in this artwork and get excited

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.370
about it, then we get enthusiastic ourselves.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:23.360
We can see that our concept is alive.”

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:28.680
Rain in the morning forced the guests to retreat to farmer Dietrich's mountain hut.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.400
The farm's eggs, milk and ham are on the breakfast menu.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.639
All the food is locally sourced.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:38.650
"It's a dream and than you wake up in the
morning and it's not a dream.”

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:39.770
“It was quite an experience.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:43.520
I actually slept amazingly well, the bed was super comfortable.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.030
So it was very nice.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.159
There was a bit of mosquitos, but it's fine.

00:04:47.159 --> 00:04:49.680
You get used to it."

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.720
The artists have turned down commercial offers for their concept - including one bid worth

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.050
millions.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:58.080
They say they want to leave the hotel's future open.

